# Contract artifacts are hash-verified. Git must not touch their bytes.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows stores LF in the blob while the
# working tree holds CRLF. scripts/sync_contract.py then writes a sidecar
# recording the CRLF hash, Linux CI checks the file out as LF, and the
# contract-pin job fails with "does not match" on every run - a gate that
# cannot pass on any platform but the one that generated it.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion, so the bytes are identical in the
# blob, on Windows, and on the CI runner.
contract/*.json -text
contract/*.sha256 -text
contract/testvectors/* -text
